mandel-recover.m's zoom with its places spawned at the host
(docs/INPROGRESS.md, Failure, step 4, D1): with no faults, and with
MERK_FAULTS failing places at random, whose chunks the coordinator gives
back out to new places, it gives mandel-places.m's iterations and checksum
(mandel-places.test) on 64 pixels square in tiles of 8 for 12 frames, with
one, three and four places, chunks of 1 and 4, at -O0 and -O2, and with
the tiles' loops on the host's threads. With no restarts, a lost place ends
the run.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-registered-target, libomp
RUN: merkc -O0 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/mandel/mandel-recover.m -o %t0
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-archs %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/mandel/mandel-recover.m -o %t.omp

RUN: %libomp-env MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=12 MANDEL_PLACES=3 %t0 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=SMALL,NONE
RUN: %libomp-env MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=12 MANDEL_PLACES=3 MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 MERK_FAULTS="seed=9 mtbf=2 fail=order count=30" %t0 host 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=SMALL,FREED
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=12 MANDEL_PLACES=1 %t.omp host | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=SMALL,NONE
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=12 MANDEL_PLACES=4 MERK_FAULTS="seed=1 mtbf=2 fail=order count=40" %t.omp host 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SMALL
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=12 MANDEL_PLACES=1 MERK_FAULTS="seed=2 mtbf=2 fail=order count=40" %t.omp host 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SMALL
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=12 MANDEL_PLACES=4 MANDEL_CHUNK=1 MERK_FAULTS="seed=3 mtbf=2 fail=order count=40" %t.omp host 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SMALL
SMALL: Iterations: 10601425
SMALL-NEXT: Checksum: 63198496
NONE-NEXT: Places lost: 0
NONE-NEXT: Tiles given back: 0
FREED: Merkurius runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed

With a collection at each allocation and the roots checked at each
safepoint, with no faults and with places failing. Each run of the
coordinator, whose loop reads a field of its frame state through a phi of
the field's address in the first frame's static term and in a cell,
checked that phi as a frame state of its own, and failed by chance; the
runs repeat.
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations %S/../../benchmarks/mandel/mandel-recover.m -o %t2
RUN: env MERK_GC_EVERY_ALLOC=1 MERK_CHECK_ROOTS=1 MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=3 %t2 host 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHECKED
RUN: env MERK_GC_EVERY_ALLOC=1 MERK_CHECK_ROOTS=1 MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=3 %t2 host 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHECKED
RUN: env MERK_GC_EVERY_ALLOC=1 MERK_CHECK_ROOTS=1 MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=3 %t2 host 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHECKED
RUN: env MERK_GC_EVERY_ALLOC=1 MERK_CHECK_ROOTS=1 MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=3 %t2 host 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHECKED
RUN: env MERK_GC_EVERY_ALLOC=1 MERK_CHECK_ROOTS=1 MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=3 MERK_FAULTS="seed=5 mtbf=2 fail=order count=10" %t2 host 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHECKED
RUN: env MERK_GC_EVERY_ALLOC=1 MERK_CHECK_ROOTS=1 MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=3 MERK_FAULTS="seed=6 mtbf=2 fail=order count=10" %t2 host 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHECKED
CHECKED: Iterations: 2017213
CHECKED-NEXT: Checksum: 5015620

A place that is lost with no restarts left, at the first fault. The fault
may hit the place between its spawn and its monitor, which the monitor
reports as noproc, as Erlang's does.
RUN: %libomp-env MANDEL_SIZE=64 MANDEL_TILE=8 MANDEL_FRAMES=1000 MANDEL_PLACES=3 MANDEL_RESTARTS=0 MERK_FAULTS="seed=4 mtbf=2 fail=order count=1" not %t0 host 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LOST
LOST: Place {{[0-2]}} ended, {{injected|noproc}}, with no restarts left.

RUN: %libomp-env MANDEL_TILE=12 not %t0 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=USAGE
RUN: %libomp-env MANDEL_RESTARTS=-1 not %t0 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=USAGE
USAGE: MANDEL_TILE must be a power of two that divides MANDEL_SIZE, MANDEL_FRAMES, MANDEL_PLACES and MANDEL_CHUNK at least 1, and MANDEL_RESTARTS at least 0.
